id     = "pose-own-curve"
about  = """A finding of round 4 (docs/decisions.md pose-transition): `exit { opacity: 0
~ ease(linear, 200ms) }` parsed, and its `~` was never read: the exit faded on
`$motion.effects`, the prop's default. design.md defines `~` per prop ("Override
per prop with `~`") and a pose as where a node moves from or to, so a `~` inside
a pose block, or on `enter:`/`exit:`, is now a load error (`check::pose_transition`,
whose fix takes the `~` out and whose help puts it on the node's own prop). This
is that help's form: the box's own `opacity: 1 ~ ease(linear, 200ms)` fades its
exit linearly over 200 ms (12 ticks), drawn last at its pose (`vanish` pop-out),
and the run rests two ticks later, once the frame that unmounts it has drawn."""
screen = { width = 200, scale = 1.0 }
hz     = 60

=== shell.strand
state shown = true
bar Top {
  height: 30
  bg: #1e2127
  row { id: strip; height: 24; gap: 6; align: center; pad: 0, 8
    box { id: lead; width: 16; height: 12; radius: 3; bg: #5c6370 }
    if shown {
      box { id: fader; width: 16; height: 12; radius: 3; bg: #98c379
            opacity: 1 ~ ease(linear, 200ms); exit { opacity: 0 } }
    }
  }
}

=== steps
rest
mark leave
set shown false
intend #fader exits
rest max 14
expect hidden #fader
expect still #lead
